  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Heat 1 tablespoon butter in a pot and soften the finely chopped onion. Add the barley and season lightly with pepper. Add half the hot stock and the garlic and keep cooking, stirring, until the liquid is absorbed. Add the remaining stock and cook until the barley is tender."
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile heat the olive oil in a frying pan and saute the quartered button mushrooms and the shimeji. Near the end of the barley cooking, add the mushrooms and porcini powder to the pot."
    },
    {
      "text": "Finish by stirring in the remaining butter."
    },
    {
      "text": "To serve, place the grizotto in the centre of each plate and top with blanched asparagus, very thinly sliced shallot and pea shoots."
    }
  ]
